From: TDVP Platform <platform@tdvp.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] gtkgreet: do not reinitialize an existing layer window

gtkgreet's monitor configure path can be invoked more than once for the same
GtkWindow after the K230 output's initial 90-degree transform is committed.
gtk-layer-shell explicitly requires gtk_layer_init_for_window() to run before
the window is mapped; a second call therefore emits a critical assertion and
leaves the greeter surface unusable. Keep the layer-shell greeter (it is the
correct no-decoration, full-output role), but only create that role once.

gtk_layer_is_layer_window() has been public since gtk-layer-shell 0.5 and is
provided by the locked 0.8 dependency.

Signed-off-by: TDVP Platform <platform@tdvp.invalid>
---
 gtkgreet/window.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/gtkgreet/window.c b/gtkgreet/window.c
index 4095f8a..44b3099 100644
--- a/gtkgreet/window.c
+++ b/gtkgreet/window.c
@@ -295,7 +295,8 @@ void window_swap_focus(struct Window *win, struct Window *old) {
 
 void window_configure(struct Window *w) {
 #ifdef LAYER_SHELL
-    if (gtkgreet->use_layer_shell) {
+    if (gtkgreet->use_layer_shell &&
+            !gtk_layer_is_layer_window(GTK_WINDOW(w->window))) {
         window_setup_layershell(w);
     }
 #endif
